 "title": "The Book of the Dead",
 "dates": "Sunday, November 1 – Tuesday, November 3, 2009",
 "logline": "On All Souls the dead get their names written down, the Saints go seven and oh, and a phone call to New Orleans keeps two people on a stairwell until it gets light.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "On the beach at Campus Point, Wes showed you a ring on his phone. “Don’t say nothing to her.” He asked you to take care of her. You drank instead of answering — and you told her so.",
   "if": "knows_wes_ring && e10_cor_truth"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the porch above Lucia: “Not to be the one who wrecks anything.” “Me neither.”",
   "if": "e11_decided==\"wreck\""
  },
  {
   "text": "When the party chanted American Gothic, you brought Becca up the stairs yourself. “I’m with Maria.”",
   "if": "e12_stairs==\"becca\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At the Point, Theo at the wall: “Don’t. Okay? Just — not there.” Then Lena asked if anybody was up there. You said just the cross.",
   "if": "saw_theo_wall && e12_told==\"cross\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Under a streetlight on Seacliff: “If God has to push me off a cliff to save me, I don’t want it that way. I want to be *asked*.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the last minute of the extra hour you took off the hat. She put it back on your head. “It’s two o’clock.”",
   "if": "e12_hat==\"off\""
  }
 ],
